   Society for their assistance in accessing Ella Baker's papers; Center
   for the Study of American Politics at Yale University},
Funding-Text = {This article is largely the product of my conversations about organizing
   with Jasson Perez, whose knowledge, encouragement, and insight inspired
   me to undertake this reading of Ella Baker's praxis. It has benefitted
   from generous feedback at various stages by current and former members
   of the Yale Political Theory Women's Writing group, including Nica
   Siegel, Alyssa Battistoni, Erin Pineda, Joy Wang, Naomi Scheinerman,
   Demi Moore, Stephanie Almeida, Anne Mishkind, and Isabelle Laurenzi. I
   received careful comments on earlier drafts from Karuna Mantena, Noreen
   Khawaja, Helene Landemore, Michael Denning, James Scott, Daniel Denvir,
   Laura Grattan, Deva Woodly, Samuel Bagg, Aaron Greenberg, Isak Tranvik,
   Mark Cladis, Andre Willis, and participants in the Religion and Critical
   Thought Colloquium at Brown University, the Religion and Modernity
   Workshop at Yale University, and the Harvard Symposium on the Ethics and
   Practice of Dissent. The three anonymous reviewers and the APSR's
   editors offered enormously helpful criticisms and suggestions. Finally,
   I am grateful to the archivists at the Schomburg Center for Research in
   Black Culture and the Wisconsin Historical Society for their assistance
   in accessing Ella Baker's papers and to the Institute for Social and
   Policy Studies and the Center for the Study of American Politics at Yale
   University for a generous grant that facilitated this research.},
